\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Probing a retained field with a real source}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{For the retained coordinate #{x} in \ref{fdip-0047}, a linear
source multiplies the weight by #{\ue^{tx}}. Differentiating this
factor at #{t=0} produces powers of #{x}; the formal logarithm in
that example combines the moments into its connected four-point
function. The exact marginal in \ref{fdip-00GJ} supplies a positive
law at every nonnegative coupling. How can the formal coefficients
be identified with controlled derivatives and remainders of these
actual integrals?}
